  Scenario: A request without a token is rejected                  # features/auth.feature:118
    When a client sends a GET request to "auth/me" without a token # features/steps/when_steps.py:72
    Then the response status code is 401                           # features/steps/then_steps.py:43

  @db
  Scenario: A structurally invalid token is rejected  # features/auth.feature:123
    Given the mock data is in place                   # features/steps/given_steps.py:22
    When invalid sends a GET request to "auth/me"     # features/steps/when_steps.py:48
    Then the response status code is 401              # features/steps/then_steps.py:43

  @db @jwt_secret
  Scenario: A correctly signed but expired token is rejected  # features/auth.feature:129
    Given the mock data is in place                           # features/steps/given_steps.py:22
    When expired sends a GET request to "auth/me"             # features/steps/when_steps.py:48
    Then the response status code is 401                      # features/steps/then_steps.py:43

  @db @rate_limit
  Scenario: Repeated sign-in attempts are rate limited                    # features/auth.feature:135
    Given the mock data is in place                                       # None
    When a client sends enough sign-in attempts to exhaust the rate limit # None
    Then the response status code is 429                                  # None

